    <string name="msg_terminal_keyboard_shortcuts">Ctrl+Tab: next tab\nCtrl+Shift+Tab: previous tab\nCtrl+Shift+T: new tab\nCtrl+Shift+W: close tab\nCtrl+Shift+C: copy the selection\nCtrl+Shift+V: paste\nCtrl+Shift+F: find in the terminal output\nCtrl+Shift+S: snippets\nCtrl+Shift+H: clipboard history\nCtrl+= / Ctrl+-: larger / smaller text of the current tab\nCtrl+0: the current tab at the saved text size\n\nCtrl+Alt shortcuts: N/P or ↓/↑ next/previous tab, C new tab, R rename, 1–9 tab, K keyboard, M menu, U URLs, V paste, +/- text size.\n\nTurn the Ctrl shortcuts off with terminal-keyboard-shortcuts = false in termux.properties, to send these keys to programs.</string>
